      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T07:11:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If seems like you are folding the error of invalid ID with the other error, which the responder couldn\u0027t tell the differences.\n\nFor example, the responder for `setStateEffecterEnables` should return completion code of `PLDM_BASE_CODES` defined in DSP0240, table 5, and `INVALID_EFFECTER_ID\u003d0x80` for the case of invalid ID.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 179,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 184,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "460c96a8deebfb1971302ef1a523ec4103fefad4",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "867f64d6_90063f97",
        "filename": "src/dsp/platform.c",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 184,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003057
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T05:33:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed. The decoder no longer validates the effecter ID (similar to decode_set_state_sensor_enables_req()), so the responder can return INVALID_EFFECTER_ID (0x80) for an invalid ID and ERROR_INVALID_DATA for the other invalid fields (-EPROTO). The encoder still rejects the reserved IDs 0 and 0xFFFF. This is documented in the header. Let me know if you would prefer the decoder to report an invalid ID with a distinct error code instead.",
      "parentUuid": "5cc0c685_b32ed4b4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 179,
